    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can see why you'd want to take control of it, but trust me, taking a double dose won't solve anything. In fact, it could make things worse. Lisinopril can cause orthostatic hypotension, which is a temporary drop in blood pressure when you stand up. The best way to deal with it is to take your meds as prescribed, and if the dizziness persists, you can try drinking a glass of water or having a snack before standing up. And let's be real, you're not going to pass out from a little dizziness - you're just being cautious, and that's good.",
